 {"id":"d88","date":"2026-07-24","title":"Work verbs renamed by tier: /pm-next /pm-done (requirement) + /dev-start /dev-end (leaf)","decision":"With leaf-level verbs added, the bare /next and /done were ambiguous about which tree they act on. Renamed by tier, mapping onto the two-tree architecture: PM tree (requirement) = /pm-next (pull, sole In-Progress authority) and /pm-done (complete, sole Done authority + evidence gate + attestation); dev tree (leaf) = /dev-start (begin a leaf: branch + implement-brief + In Progress) and /dev-end (complete a leaf: assume the implement loop already verified, land the PR, reconcile parent, suggest next). The dev verbs remain ERGONOMIC packaging, never authorities (no binding, never touch the PM item), preserving d82/d87. Skill dirs renamed (.claude/skills/next|done|leaf-start|leaf-done -> pm-next|pm-done|dev-start|dev-end); all refs swept across the four skills + bind/blocked/override/doc-sync, CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md section 5, loop/decomp README+TREE-REVIEW, loop/work/*.ps1 (banner/work-lib/materialize comments), the adopted way-of-work doc (17 /next + 20 /done), and the two-rhythms artifact. KNOWN LAG (not drift): the 30 Linear PM cover-sheet descriptions still say /next in a parenthetical; refreshed at first pull / next doc-sync sweep, not worth 30 MCP writes now.","evidence":"Founder ruling 2026-07-24 (\"pm-next pm-done and dev-start dev-end\"); grep-verified zero residual bare /next|/done|/leaf-* in tracked docs (Next.js migration doc excluded - unrelated framework name); skills re-registered under new names.","status":"adopted"}
 {"id":"d89","date":"2026-07-30","title":"Discovery fit-decline gets human oversight: decline-then-review","decision":"The Discovery maintainability/confidential-codebase decline was the only consequential AI judgment in v1 reaching a decision with no human in the loop, and the one nobody contests - a declined NGO simply leaves, so a miscalibrated evaluator would be invisible by construction. Inconsistent with d74 (no auto-approval exists). RULING: decline-then-review. (1) The decline reaches the NGO immediately - kind, plainly reasoned, final in the moment, no waiting state, no SLA - and its copy states that a person reads every decline and will reach out if it was wrong. (2) Every decline opens a platform-admin ops item carrying the project, the cause and the full Discovery conversation, plus an admin notification; it stays open until the founder disposes it upheld or overturned; an overturn reopens Discovery and notifies the NGO; dispositions are the decline evaluator calibration dataset, parallel to the founder-review records for the triage screener (REQ-023). (3) The decline is also a durable project record (cause, date, reshaping suggestion) - the declined project stays visible in the NGO project list, not only in chat. (4) Decline copy gains the oversight sentence. (5) LIFECYCLE RESOLVED, no tenth state: discovery_in_progress -\u003e cancelled on fit decline, actor = the Discovery fit check, the only machine-initiated cancellation in the table; funded fuel returns to general balance; no keys or volunteer exist yet. Plus ONE reverse transition - cancelled -\u003e discovery_in_progress, platform-admin only, permitted solely when disposing a fit-decline ops item as overturned, audited. Human-chosen cancellations (the NGO own, and the REQ-023 triage decline) stay irreversibly terminal. The asymmetry is deliberate: only a cancellation no human decided can be undone, which is why existing terminality tests (AT-005.5.18, AT-005.5.35) are unaffected.","evidence":"Folded into loop/out/pure-s3-req-001-006.md (REQ-004 decline-then-review bullet; REQ-005.5 two new transition rules) and loop/out/pure-s6-req-027-036.md (REQ-016 taxonomy row: decline delivered -\u003e NGO + platform admin + exactly one ops item; disposition rows). Founder ruling 2026-07-30. Design side (Discovery chat state G, ops-items screen, notification rows) re-flows top-down from these; no design files edited.","status":"folded"}
 {"id":"d90","date":"2026-07-31","title":"Cause taxonomy is self-generated and normalizing, never human-curated; causes become optional throughout","decision":"The UI design gate surfaced an unresolved question at project intake: a placeholder picker of ten hard-coded causes, flagged because the vocabulary must be shared between project intake and the volunteer profile or matching cannot compare them. RULING: (1) Causes are optional at intake and for matching - v1 matching is concierge (a human reading the problem description), so a cause is a coarse aid, never a required input. (2) The taxonomy is self-generated from text the product already has - the NGO org profile's mission, the project intake description, and the Discovery conversation. No human ever curates a cause list, not the NGO and not the founder; there is no admin taxonomy-management surface. (3) Generation must normalize, not freely invent - the load-bearing constraint. Independent per-project generation would produce synonyms for the same domain (\"food security\" / \"hunger relief\" / \"food banks\"), which would make public listings noisy and break comparison between a volunteer tagged one way and a project tagged another. The generator must see the labels that already exist and reuse one unless the need is genuinely new, in which case the vocabulary grows by itself - emergent but converging. (4) Authoritative generation happens in the Discovery pass, which already produces a structured scope - emitting 0-3 normalized cause labels is an addition to that existing AI step, not new machinery; a project shown before Discovery has run (a draft) legitimately shows none. (5) The NGO may remove a wrong label but never type a new one - correction stays possible, invention stays machine-owned. (6) Volunteers pick from the emergent set as it stands at the time - still no human curating, just choosing from what the system has generated; optional, zero allowed. (7) Public listings display whatever labels exist and nothing more - there are no cause filters in v1. Scope caution (founder-stated): this must not grow into a taxonomy-management feature, a clustering service, or an approval queue - the v1 shape is Discovery emits a few labels, reusing existing ones where they fit.","evidence":"Folded into loop/out/pure-s3-req-001-006.md (REQ-002 mission-text-as-generation-input note; REQ-003 intake no longer captures a cause field + remove-only correction; REQ-004 structured-output list gains cause labels + new cause-taxonomy-generation bullet) and loop/out/pure-s4-req-007-012.md (REQ-007 profile causes = picker from the emergent set, optional; REQ-011 open-project card cause tags = zero to three, display-only, no filter). prd-mvp.md reassembled (VERIFY OK, 0 banned words, 0 decision refs, 62 RM refs in roadmap). AT suites: at-req-003.md (+AT-003.17, reworded AT-003.02, 12->13 P0), at-req-004.md (+AT-004.58/59/60, reworded AT-004.20, 55->58 P0), at-req-007.md (+AT-007.31, 28->29 P0), at-req-011.md (same-id wording refinements to AT-011.05/11, no new P0s), at-req-002.md (cross-reference only, no new P0). Decomp manifests req-003/004/007/011 updated with matching leaves and coverage-check totals; check-tree.ps1 RESULT: ALL CHECKS PASS (30 nodes, topological order exists). Founder ruling 2026-07-31. Design side (project intake, org profile, volunteer profile, public listings) re-flows top-down from these; no design files edited.","status":"folded"}
+{"id":"d91","date":"2026-09-06","title":"The GitHub link is permanent after volunteer signup: unlink is refused","decision":"REQ-001 makes a GitHub link mandatory at volunteer signup and REQ-007 builds the volunteer profile from it, but no clause said what happens after signup, so a volunteer could unlink the identity through the auth provider and keep an account the profile no longer describes. RULING (the founder brief for the admin-operations item, unit 5): once volunteer signup is complete the GitHub link is permanent; an attempt to unlink that identity is refused and the identity stays linked. NGO accounts are not covered: their GitHub identity was never mandatory. Recovery of a volunteer who lost the GitHub account is not designed here; it is a platform-admin path for a later item. The refusal lives where the auth service deletes the identity row, so a client that bypasses the product surface is refused too.","evidence":"Folded into loop/out/pure-s3-req-001-006.md (REQ-001 sign-in bullet gains the permanence sentence); prd-mvp.md reassembled and the REQ-001 isolate re-extracted; at-req-001.md gains AT-001.41 (P0) in section A (37 to 38 P0) and the coverage-map row; loop/decomp/req-001.md gains D1.L3 with the matching verify set and the 38 total; check-tree passes. Founder brief loop/items/AI4DEV-56/brief.md, unit 5.","status":"folded"}
